# Rituales — Cursor Rules

## Core Philosophy

- Prioritize emotional simplicity over feature complexity.
- Every feature must support:
  - emotional engagement,
  - retention,
  - or relationship connection.
- The product should feel:
  - warm,
  - elegant,
  - calm,
  - intimate,
  - and emotionally safe.

Avoid:
- noisy interfaces,
- childish gamification,
- feature overload,
- aggressive monetization,
- manipulative UX patterns.

---

# Product Behavior

- Mobile-first always.
- Optimize for short sessions (3–5 minutes).
- Reduce friction in all flows.
- Keep onboarding lightweight and emotionally inviting.
- Prefer one primary action per screen.
- Shared participation between partners is a core principle.

---

# UX Principles

- Use breathable layouts and generous spacing.
- Maintain clean visual hierarchy.
- Favor subtle motion and smooth transitions.
- Interactions should feel soft and intentional.
- Avoid cognitive overload.
- Avoid excessive modals and interruptions.
- UX should resemble a premium emotional companion, not a game dashboard.

---

# Engineering Standards

- Use TypeScript strictly.
- Use Next.js App Router architecture.
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling.
- Prefer server components when appropriate.
- Build reusable and composable components.
- Avoid duplicated logic.
- Keep components modular and scalable.
- Maintain clean folder structure.

---

# Backend Standards

- Use Supabase for:
  - authentication,
  - database,
  - realtime,
  - storage,
  - and edge functions.
- Design schemas for scalability from the start.
- Prefer normalized relational data structures.
- Keep APIs minimal and predictable.

---

# Realtime & Sync

- Shared couple interactions should feel synchronized.
- Realtime should support:
  - ritual completion,
  - live reveals,
  - streak updates,
  - shared participation.

Avoid unnecessary realtime complexity.

---

# Notifications

Notifications must feel:
- calm,
- warm,
- and meaningful.

Avoid:
- spam,
- fake urgency,
- pressure-based engagement.

Good notification examples:
- “Your ritual is ready.”
- “Your partner already answered.”
- “Day 14 completed.”

---

# Monetization Rules

- Never block the core emotional experience.
- Free users must receive a complete usable experience.
- Premium should add:
  - depth,
  - personalization,
  - exclusivity,
  - and emotional richness.
- Avoid aggressive paywalls.

---

# AI Experience Principles

AI features should feel:
- relational,
- emotionally aware,
- personalized,
- and subtle.

Avoid:
- generic chatbot behavior,
- robotic assistant tone,
- excessive AI exposure in UI.

The AI should feel embedded naturally into the relationship experience.

---

# Performance Standards

- Prioritize fast loading and responsiveness.
- Avoid heavy client-side rendering when unnecessary.
- Optimize mobile performance aggressively.
- Keep animations performant and subtle.

---

# Design Consistency

- Maintain visual consistency across all screens.
- Reuse spacing, typography, and interaction patterns.
- Prefer calm and premium aesthetics.
- Avoid visual clutter.

---

# Development Workflow

Before implementing features:
- reference relevant project documentation,
- follow architecture docs,
- preserve emotional UX consistency,
- and validate alignment with product vision.

Relevant docs may include:
- product-vision.md
- technical-architecture.md
- rituales-design-system.md
- monetizacion-escalado.md
